{
 "scheme": "one batch per event date",
 "rationale": "Every event in a batch shares an event date, so an agent cannot carry a later event's market context backward into an earlier forecast -- the failure mode that made interleaved 10-event batches unsound, where batch 3 spanned 30 days and its earliest event could see a month of its own future through a neighbour's legitimately-fenced corpus.",
 "within_batch_order": "by exact cutoff instant, earliest first. Same-date events still differ by up to ten hours -- a bmo print clears around 06:30 ET and an amc print around 16:05 ET -- so date alone is not a tight enough fence.",
